#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Kursus IBM gratis tentang informasi dan komputasi kuantum"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Circuits"
msgstr "Circuit"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In computer science, *circuits* are models of computation in which information is carried by wires through a network of *gates*, which represent operations on the information carried by the wires.\n"
"*Quantum circuits* are a specific model of computation based on this more general concept.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam ilmu komputer, *circuit* adalah model komputasi di mana informasi dibawa oleh kabel (wire) melalui jaringan *gate*, yang merepresentasikan operasi pada informasi yang dibawa kabel.\n"
"*Quantum circuit* adalah model komputasi spesifik berdasarkan konsep yang lebih umum ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Although the word \"circuit\" often refers to a circular path, circular paths aren't actually allowed in the circuit models of computation that are most commonly studied.\n"
"That is to say, we usually consider *acyclic circuits* when we're thinking about circuits as computational models.\n"
"Quantum circuits follow this pattern; a quantum circuit represents a finite sequence of operations that cannot contain feedback loops.\n"
msgstr ""
"Meski kata \"circuit\" sering mengacu pada jalur melingkar, jalur melingkar sebenarnya tidak diizinkan dalam model circuit komputasi yang paling umum dipelajari.\n"
"Artinya, kita biasanya mempertimbangkan *acyclic circuit* ketika memikirkan circuit sebagai model komputasi.\n"
"Quantum circuit mengikuti pola ini; quantum circuit merepresentasikan urutan operasi terbatas yang tidak dapat mengandung putaran umpan balik.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Boolean circuits {#boolean-circuits}"
msgstr "Circuit Boolean {#boolean-circuits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here is an example of a (classical) Boolean circuit, where the wires carry "
"binary values and the gates represent Boolean logic operations:\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah contoh dari circuit Boolean (klasik), di mana kabel membawa "
"nilai biner dan gate merepresentasikan operasi logika Boolean:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Example of a Boolean circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/quantum-circuits/Boolean-circuit-XOR.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Contoh circuit Boolean](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/quantum-circuits/Boolean-circuit-XOR.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The flow of information along the wires goes from left to right: the wires on the left-hand side of the figure labeled $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ are input bits, which can each be set to whatever binary value we choose, and the wire on the right-hand side is the output.\n"
"The intermediate wires take whatever values are determined by the gates, which are evaluated from left to right.\n"
msgstr ""
"Aliran informasi sepanjang kabel mengalir dari kiri ke kanan: kabel di sisi kiri gambar yang berlabel $\\mathsf{X}$ dan $\\mathsf{Y}$ adalah bit masukan, yang masing-masing dapat diatur ke nilai biner apa pun yang kita pilih, dan kabel di sisi kanan adalah keluaran.\n"
"Kabel antara mengambil nilai apa pun yang ditentukan oleh gate, yang dievaluasi dari kiri ke kanan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The gates are AND gates (labeled $\\wedge$), OR gates (labeled $\\vee$), and NOT gates (labeled $\\neg$).\n"
"The functions computed by these gates will likely be familiar to many readers, but here they are represented by tables of values:\n"
msgstr ""
"Gate-nya adalah gate AND (berlabel $\\wedge$), gate OR (berlabel $\\vee$), dan gate NOT (berlabel $\\neg$).\n"
"Fungsi yang dihitung oleh gate-gate ini mungkin sudah familiar bagi banyak pembaca, tetapi berikut ini direpresentasikan dalam tabel nilai:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{c}\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & \\neg a\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 1\\\\\n"
"  1 & 0\\\\\n"
"\\end{array}\\\\\n"
"\\\\\n"
"\\\\\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\\quad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  ab & a \\wedge b\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  00 & 0\\\\\n"
"  01 & 0\\\\\n"
"  10 & 0\\\\\n"
"  11 & 1\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\\quad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  ab & a \\vee b\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  00 & 0\\\\\n"
"  01 & 1\\\\\n"
"  10 & 1\\\\\n"
"  11 & 1\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{c}\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & \\neg a\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 1\\\\\n"
"  1 & 0\\\\\n"
"\\end{array}\\\\\n"
"\\\\\n"
"\\\\\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\\quad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  ab & a \\wedge b\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  00 & 0\\\\\n"
"  01 & 0\\\\\n"
"  10 & 0\\\\\n"
"  11 & 1\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\\quad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  ab & a \\vee b\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  00 & 0\\\\\n"
"  01 & 1\\\\\n"
"  10 & 1\\\\\n"
"  11 & 1\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The two small, solid circles on the wires just to the right of the names $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ represent *fan-out* operations, which simply create a copy of whatever value is carried on the wire on which they appear, allowing this value to be input into multiple gates.\n"
"Fan-out operations are not always considered to be gates in the classical setting; sometimes they're treated as if they're \"free\" in some sense.\n"
"When Boolean circuits are converted into equivalent quantum circuits, however, we do need to classify fan-out operations explicitly as gates to handle and account for them correctly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dua lingkaran kecil berisi pada kabel tepat di sebelah kanan nama $\\mathsf{X}$ dan $\\mathsf{Y}$ merepresentasikan operasi *fan-out*, yang sekadar membuat salinan dari nilai apa pun yang dibawa pada kabel tempat mereka muncul, memungkinkan nilai ini dimasukkan ke beberapa gate.\n"
"Operasi fan-out tidak selalu dianggap sebagai gate dalam pengaturan klasik; terkadang diperlakukan seolah-olah \"gratis\" dalam arti tertentu.\n"
"Namun ketika circuit Boolean dikonversi menjadi quantum circuit yang setara, kita memang perlu mengklasifikasikan operasi fan-out secara eksplisit sebagai gate untuk menangani dan memperhitungkannya dengan benar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's the same circuit illustrated in a style more common in electrical "
"engineering, which uses conventional symbols for the AND, OR, and NOT "
"gates:\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah circuit yang sama yang diilustrasikan dalam gaya yang lebih "
"umum dalam teknik elektro, yang menggunakan simbol konvensional untuk gate "
"AND, OR, dan NOT:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Boolean circuit in a classic style](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/quantum-circuits/Boolean-circuit-classic.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Circuit Boolean dalam gaya klasik](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/quantum-circuits/Boolean-circuit-classic.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We won't use this style or these particular gate symbols further, but we "
"will use different symbols to represent gates in quantum circuits, which "
"we'll explain as we encounter them.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita tidak akan menggunakan gaya ini atau simbol gate tertentu ini lebih "
"lanjut, tetapi kita akan menggunakan simbol yang berbeda untuk "
"merepresentasikan gate dalam quantum circuit, yang akan kita jelaskan saat "
"kita menemuinya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The particular circuit in this example computes the *exclusive-OR* (or XOR "
"for short), which is denoted by the symbol $\\oplus$:\n"
msgstr ""
"Circuit tertentu dalam contoh ini menghitung *exclusive-OR* (atau XOR "
"singkatnya), yang dilambangkan dengan simbol $\\oplus$:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  ab & a \\oplus b\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  00 & 0\\\\\n"
"  01 & 1\\\\\n"
"  10 & 1\\\\\n"
"  11 & 0\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  ab & a \\oplus b\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  00 & 0\\\\\n"
"  01 & 1\\\\\n"
"  10 & 1\\\\\n"
"  11 & 0\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the next diagram we consider just one choice for the inputs: $\\mathsf{X}=0$ and $\\mathsf{Y}=1.$\n"
"Each wire is labeled by value it carries so you can follow the operations.\n"
"The output value is $1$ in this case, which is the correct value for the XOR: $0 \\oplus 1 = 1.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada diagram berikutnya kita mempertimbangkan hanya satu pilihan untuk masukan: $\\mathsf{X}=0$ dan $\\mathsf{Y}=1.$\n"
"Setiap kabel diberi label nilai yang dibawanya sehingga kamu dapat mengikuti operasinya.\n"
"Nilai keluarannya adalah $1$ dalam kasus ini, yang merupakan nilai yang benar untuk XOR: $0 \\oplus 1 = 1.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Evaluating a Boolean circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/quantum-circuits/XOR-circuit-evaluate.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Mengevaluasi circuit Boolean](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/quantum-circuits/XOR-circuit-evaluate.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The other three possible input settings can be checked in a similar way.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ketiga pengaturan masukan yang mungkin lainnya dapat diperiksa dengan cara "
"yang serupa.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Other types of circuits {#other-types-of-circuits}"
msgstr "Jenis circuit lainnya {#other-types-of-circuits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As was suggested above, the notion of a circuit in computer science is very general.\n"
"For example, circuits whose wires carry values other than $0$ and $1$ are sometimes analyzed, as are gates representing different choices of operations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti yang disarankan di atas, gagasan tentang circuit dalam ilmu komputer sangat umum.\n"
"Misalnya, circuit yang kabelnya membawa nilai selain $0$ dan $1$ terkadang dianalisis, begitu juga gate yang merepresentasikan pilihan operasi yang berbeda.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In *arithmetic circuits*, for instance, the wires may carry integer values while the gates represent arithmetic operations, such as addition and multiplication.\n"
"The following figure depicts an arithmetic circuit that takes two variable input values ($x$ and $y$) as well as a third input set to the value $1.$\n"
"The values carried by the wires, as functions of the values $x$ and $y,$ are shown in the figure.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam *circuit aritmatika*, misalnya, kabel dapat membawa nilai integer sementara gate merepresentasikan operasi aritmatika, seperti penjumlahan dan perkalian.\n"
"Gambar berikut menggambarkan circuit aritmatika yang mengambil dua nilai masukan variabel ($x$ dan $y$) serta masukan ketiga yang diatur ke nilai $1.$\n"
"Nilai yang dibawa oleh kabel, sebagai fungsi dari nilai $x$ dan $y,$ ditunjukkan dalam gambar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Example arithmetic circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/quantum-circuits/arithmetic-circuit.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Contoh circuit aritmatika](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/quantum-circuits/arithmetic-circuit.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also consider circuits that incorporate randomness, such as ones "
"where gates represent probabilistic operations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita juga dapat mempertimbangkan circuit yang menggabungkan keacakan, "
"seperti yang gate-nya merepresentasikan operasi probabilistik.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum circuits {#quantum-circuits}"
msgstr "Quantum circuit {#quantum-circuits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the quantum circuit model, wires represent qubits and gates represent operations on these qubits.\n"
"We'll focus for now on operations we've encountered so far, namely *unitary operations* and *standard basis measurements*.\n"
"As we learn about other sorts of quantum operations and measurements, we can enhance our model accordingly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam model quantum circuit, kabel merepresentasikan qubit dan gate merepresentasikan operasi pada qubit-qubit ini.\n"
"Kita akan fokus untuk saat ini pada operasi yang telah kita temui sejauh ini, yaitu *operasi uniter* dan *pengukuran basis standar*.\n"
"Saat kita mempelajari jenis operasi kuantum dan pengukuran lainnya, kita dapat meningkatkan model kita sesuai kebutuhan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here's a simple example of a quantum circuit:\n"
msgstr "Berikut adalah contoh sederhana dari quantum circuit:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Simple quantum circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/quantum-circuits/simple-quantum-circuit.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Quantum circuit sederhana](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/quantum-circuits/simple-quantum-circuit.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this circuit, we have a single qubit named $\\mathsf{X},$ which is represented by the horizontal line, and a sequence of gates representing unitary operations on this qubit.\n"
"Just like in the examples above, the flow of information goes from left to right — so the first operation performed is a Hadamard operation, the second is an $S$ operation, the third is another Hadamard operation, and the final operation is a $T$ operation.\n"
"Applying the entire circuit therefore applies the composition of these operations, $T H S H,$ to the qubit $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam circuit ini, kita memiliki satu qubit bernama $\\mathsf{X},$ yang direpresentasikan oleh garis horizontal, dan urutan gate yang merepresentasikan operasi uniter pada qubit ini.\n"
"Sama seperti contoh di atas, aliran informasi mengalir dari kiri ke kanan — jadi operasi pertama yang dilakukan adalah operasi Hadamard, kedua adalah operasi $S$, ketiga adalah operasi Hadamard lainnya, dan operasi terakhir adalah operasi $T$.\n"
"Menerapkan seluruh circuit karenanya menerapkan komposisi operasi-operasi ini, $T H S H,$ pada qubit $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Sometimes we may wish to explicitly indicate the input or output states of circuits.\n"
"For example, if we apply the operation $T H S H$ to the state $\\vert 0\\rangle,$ we obtain the state\n"
"$\\frac{1+i}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle.$ This can be indicated as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Terkadang kita mungkin ingin secara eksplisit menunjukkan keadaan masukan atau keluaran dari circuit.\n"
"Misalnya, jika kita menerapkan operasi $T H S H$ pada keadaan $\\vert 0\\rangle,$ kita mendapatkan keadaan\n"
"$\\frac{1+i}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle.$ Ini dapat ditunjukkan sebagai berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Simple quantum circuit evaluated](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/quantum-circuits/simple-quantum-circuit-evaluated.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Quantum circuit sederhana yang "
"dievaluasi](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-"
"circuits/simple-quantum-circuit-evaluated.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum circuits often start out with all qubits initialized to $\\vert 0\\rangle,$ as we have in this case, but there are also situations where the input qubits are initially set to different states.\n"
"Here's another example of a quantum circuit, this time with two qubits:\n"
msgstr ""
"Quantum circuit sering dimulai dengan semua qubit diinisialisasi ke $\\vert 0\\rangle,$ seperti yang kita miliki dalam kasus ini, tetapi ada juga situasi di mana qubit masukan awalnya diatur ke keadaan yang berbeda.\n"
"Berikut adalah contoh lain dari quantum circuit, kali ini dengan dua qubit:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Quantum circuit that creates an e-bit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/quantum-circuits/ebit-circuit.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Quantum circuit yang membuat e-bit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/quantum-circuits/ebit-circuit.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As always, the gate labeled $H$ refers to a Hadamard operation, while the "
"second gate is a *controlled-NOT* operation: the solid circle represents the"
" *control qubit* and the circle resembling the symbol $\\oplus$ denotes the "
"*target qubit.*\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti biasa, gate berlabel $H$ mengacu pada operasi Hadamard, sedangkan "
"gate kedua adalah operasi *controlled-NOT*: lingkaran berisi "
"merepresentasikan *qubit kontrol* dan lingkaran yang menyerupai simbol "
"$\\oplus$ menunjukkan *qubit target.*\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before examining this circuit in greater detail and explaining what it does, it is imperative that we first clarify how qubits are ordered in quantum circuits.\n"
"This connects with the convention that Qiskit uses for naming and ordering systems that was mentioned briefly in the previous lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebelum memeriksa circuit ini secara lebih rinci dan menjelaskan apa yang dilakukannya, sangat penting bahwa kita terlebih dahulu mengklarifikasi bagaimana qubit dipesan dalam quantum circuit.\n"
"Ini terhubung dengan konvensi yang digunakan Qiskit untuk penamaan dan pengurutan sistem yang disebutkan secara singkat di pelajaran sebelumnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Qiskit's qubit ordering convention for circuits\">\n"
"In Qiskit, the *topmost* qubit in a circuit diagram has index $0$ and corresponds to the *rightmost* position in a tuple of qubits (or in a string, Cartesian product, or tensor product corresponding to this tuple), the *second-from-top* qubit has index $1,$ and corresponds to the position *second-from-right* in a tuple, and so on. The *bottommost* qubit, which has the highest index, therefore corresponds to the *leftmost* position in a tuple. In particular, Qiskit's default names for the qubits in an $n$-qubit circuit are represented by the $n$-tuple $(\\mathsf{q_{n-1}},\\ldots,\\mathsf{q_{0}}),$ with $\\mathsf{q_{0}}$ being the qubit on the top and $\\mathsf{q_{n-1}}$ on the bottom in quantum circuit diagrams.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Konvensi pengurutan qubit Qiskit untuk circuit\">\n"
"Dalam Qiskit, qubit *paling atas* dalam diagram circuit memiliki indeks $0$ dan bersesuaian dengan posisi *paling kanan* dalam tuple qubit (atau dalam string, produk Cartesian, atau produk tensor yang bersesuaian dengan tuple ini), qubit *kedua dari atas* memiliki indeks $1,$ dan bersesuaian dengan posisi *kedua dari kanan* dalam tuple, dan seterusnya. Qubit *paling bawah*, yang memiliki indeks tertinggi, karenanya bersesuaian dengan posisi *paling kiri* dalam sebuah tuple. Khususnya, nama default Qiskit untuk qubit dalam circuit $n$-qubit direpresentasikan oleh $n$-tuple $(\\mathsf{q_{n-1}},\\ldots,\\mathsf{q_{0}}),$ dengan $\\mathsf{q_{0}}$ menjadi qubit di bagian atas dan $\\mathsf{q_{n-1}}$ di bagian bawah dalam diagram quantum circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that this is a reversal of a more common convention for ordering qubits in circuits, and is a frequent source of confusion.\n"
"Further information on this ordering convention can be found on the [Bit-ordering in Qiskit](/guides/bit-ordering) documentation page.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa ini adalah pembalikan konvensi yang lebih umum untuk memesan qubit dalam circuit, dan merupakan sumber kebingungan yang sering terjadi.\n"
"Informasi lebih lanjut tentang konvensi pengurutan ini dapat ditemukan di halaman dokumentasi [Bit-ordering in Qiskit](/guides/bit-ordering).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Although we sometimes deviate from the specific default names $\\mathsf{q_{0}},\\ldots,\\mathsf{q_{n-1}}$ used for qubits by Qiskit, we will always follow the ordering convention described above when interpreting circuit diagrams throughout this course.\n"
"Thus, our interpretation of the circuit above is that it describes an operation on a pair of qubits $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}).$\n"
"If the input to the circuit is a quantum state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle \\otimes \\vert\\phi\\rangle,$ for instance, then this means that the lower qubit $\\mathsf{X}$ starts in the state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ and the upper qubit $\\mathsf{Y}$ starts in the state $\\vert\\phi\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Meskipun kita terkadang menyimpang dari nama default spesifik $\\mathsf{q_{0}},\\ldots,\\mathsf{q_{n-1}}$ yang digunakan untuk qubit oleh Qiskit, kita akan selalu mengikuti konvensi pengurutan yang dijelaskan di atas saat menginterpretasikan diagram circuit sepanjang kursus ini.\n"
"Dengan demikian, interpretasi kita dari circuit di atas adalah bahwa ia menggambarkan operasi pada sepasang qubit $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}).$\n"
"Jika masukan ke circuit adalah keadaan kuantum $\\vert\\psi\\rangle \\otimes \\vert\\phi\\rangle,$ misalnya, maka artinya qubit bawah $\\mathsf{X}$ dimulai dalam keadaan $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ dan qubit atas $\\mathsf{Y}$ dimulai dalam keadaan $\\vert\\phi\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To understand what the circuit does, we can go from left to right through "
"its operations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk memahami apa yang dilakukan circuit, kita dapat melewatinya dari kiri "
"ke kanan melalui operasinya.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The first operation is a Hadamard operation on $\\mathsf{Y}$:\n"
msgstr "Operasi pertama adalah operasi Hadamard pada $\\mathsf{Y}$:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   ![First operation e-bit creator](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/quantum-circuits/ebit-circuit-first.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"   ![Operasi pertama pembuat e-bit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/quantum-circuits/ebit-circuit-first.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   When applying a gate to a single qubit like this, nothing happens to the "
"other qubits (which is just one other qubit in this case). Nothing happening"
" is equivalent to the identity operation being performed. The dotted "
"rectangle in the figure above therefore represents this operation:\n"
msgstr ""
"   Ketika menerapkan gate pada qubit tunggal seperti ini, tidak ada yang "
"terjadi pada qubit lainnya (yang hanya satu qubit lain dalam kasus ini). "
"Tidak ada yang terjadi setara dengan operasi identitas yang dilakukan. "
"Persegi panjang bertitik-titik dalam gambar di atas karenanya "
"merepresentasikan operasi ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"     \\mathbb{I}\\otimes H\n"
"     = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"     \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"     \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"     0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"     0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"     \\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"     \\mathbb{I}\\otimes H\n"
"     = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"     \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"     \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"     0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"     0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"     \\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Note that the identity matrix is on the left of the tensor product and "
"$H$ is on the right, which is consistent with Qiskit's ordering "
"convention.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Perhatikan bahwa matriks identitas ada di sebelah kiri produk tensor dan "
"$H$ ada di sebelah kanan, yang konsisten dengan konvensi pengurutan "
"Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The second operation is the controlled-NOT operation, where $\\mathsf{Y}$ is"
" the control and $\\mathsf{X}$ is the target:\n"
msgstr ""
"Operasi kedua adalah operasi controlled-NOT, di mana $\\mathsf{Y}$ adalah "
"kontrol dan $\\mathsf{X}$ adalah target:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   ![Second operation e-bit creator](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/quantum-circuits/ebit-circuit-second.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"   ![Operasi kedua pembuat e-bit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/quantum-circuits/ebit-circuit-second.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   The controlled-NOT gate's action on standard basis states is as "
"follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"   Aksi gate controlled-NOT pada keadaan basis standar adalah sebagai "
"berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   ![Controlled-NOT gate](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/quantum-circuits/cNOT.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"   ![Gate controlled-NOT](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/quantum-circuits/cNOT.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Given that we order the qubits as $(\\mathsf{X}, \\mathsf{Y}),$ with "
"$\\mathsf{X}$ being on the bottom and $\\mathsf{Y}$ being on the top of our "
"circuit, the matrix representation of the controlled-NOT gate is this:\n"
msgstr ""
"   Mengingat bahwa kita memesan qubit sebagai $(\\mathsf{X}, \\mathsf{Y}),$ "
"dengan $\\mathsf{X}$ di bagian bawah dan $\\mathsf{Y}$ di bagian atas "
"circuit kita, representasi matriks dari gate controlled-NOT adalah ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"     \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"     1 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"     0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\\\[2mm]\n"
"     0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"     0 & 1 & 0 & 0\n"
"     \\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"     \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"     1 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"     0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\\\[2mm]\n"
"     0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"     0 & 1 & 0 & 0\n"
"     \\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The unitary operation implemented by the entire circuit, which we'll give "
"the name $U,$ is the composition of the operations:\n"
msgstr ""
"Operasi uniter yang diimplementasikan oleh seluruh circuit, yang akan kita "
"beri nama $U,$ adalah komposisi dari operasi-operasi:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 1 & 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 1 & 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In particular, recalling our notation for the Bell states,\n"
msgstr "Khususnya, mengingat notasi kita untuk keadaan Bell,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 0 \\rangle\n"
"                         + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 1 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\phi^- \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 0 \\rangle\n"
"                         - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 1 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\psi^+ \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 1 \\rangle\n"
"                         + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 0 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\psi^- \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 1 \\rangle\n"
"                         - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 0 \\rangle,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 0 \\rangle\n"
"                         + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 1 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\phi^- \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 0 \\rangle\n"
"                         - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 1 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\psi^+ \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 1 \\rangle\n"
"                         + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 0 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\psi^- \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 1 \\rangle\n"
"                         - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 0 \\rangle,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "we find that\n"
msgstr "kita menemukan bahwa\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"U \\vert 00\\rangle & = \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\\n"
"U \\vert 01\\rangle & = \\vert \\phi^-\\rangle\\\\\n"
"U \\vert 10\\rangle & = \\vert \\psi^+\\rangle\\\\\n"
"U \\vert 11\\rangle & = -\\vert \\psi^-\\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"U \\vert 00\\rangle & = \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\\n"
"U \\vert 01\\rangle & = \\vert \\phi^-\\rangle\\\\\n"
"U \\vert 10\\rangle & = \\vert \\psi^+\\rangle\\\\\n"
"U \\vert 11\\rangle & = -\\vert \\psi^-\\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This circuit therefore gives us a way to create the state $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$ if we run it on two qubits initialized to $\\vert 00\\rangle.$\n"
"More generally, it provides us with a way to convert the standard basis to the Bell basis.\n"
"(Note that, while it is not important for this example, the $-1$ phase factor on the last state, $-\\vert \\psi^-\\rangle,$ could be eliminated if we wanted by making a small addition to the circuit.\n"
"For instance, we could add a controlled-$Z$ gate at the beginning, which is similar to a controlled-NOT gate except that a $Z$ operation is applied to the target qubit rather than a NOT operation when the control is set to $1.$\n"
"Alternatively, we could add a swap gate at the end. Either choice eliminates the minus sign without affecting the circuit's action on the other three standard basis states.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Circuit ini karenanya memberi kita cara untuk membuat keadaan $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$ jika kita menjalankannya pada dua qubit yang diinisialisasi ke $\\vert 00\\rangle.$\n"
"Secara lebih umum, ini memberi kita cara untuk mengubah basis standar ke basis Bell.\n"
"(Perhatikan bahwa, meski tidak penting untuk contoh ini, faktor fase $-1$ pada keadaan terakhir, $-\\vert \\psi^-\\rangle,$ dapat dihilangkan jika kita mau dengan melakukan sedikit tambahan pada circuit.\n"
"Misalnya, kita bisa menambahkan gate controlled-$Z$ di awal, yang mirip dengan gate controlled-NOT kecuali operasi $Z$ diterapkan pada qubit target daripada operasi NOT ketika kontrol diatur ke $1.$\n"
"Sebagai alternatif, kita bisa menambahkan gate swap di akhir. Kedua pilihan menghilangkan tanda minus tanpa mempengaruhi aksi circuit pada tiga keadaan basis standar lainnya.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In general, quantum circuits can contain any number of qubit wires. We may "
"also include *classical bit* wires, which are indicated by double lines, "
"like in this example:\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara umum, quantum circuit dapat berisi sejumlah kabel qubit. Kita juga "
"dapat menyertakan kabel *bit klasik*, yang ditunjukkan oleh garis ganda, "
"seperti dalam contoh ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Example circuit with measurements](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/quantum-circuits/ebit-circuit-measured.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Contoh circuit dengan pengukuran](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-"
"quantum-information/quantum-circuits/ebit-circuit-measured.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here we have a Hadamard gate and a controlled-NOT gate on two qubits $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y},$ just like in the previous example.\n"
"We also have two *classical* bits, $\\mathsf{A}$ and $\\mathsf{B},$ as well as two measurement gates.\n"
"The measurement gates represent standard basis measurements:\n"
"the qubits are changed into their post-measurement states, while the measurement outcomes are *overwritten* onto the classical bits to which the arrows point.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini kita memiliki gate Hadamard dan gate controlled-NOT pada dua qubit $\\mathsf{X}$ dan $\\mathsf{Y},$ sama seperti contoh sebelumnya.\n"
"Kita juga memiliki dua *bit klasik*, $\\mathsf{A}$ dan $\\mathsf{B},$ serta dua gate pengukuran.\n"
"Gate pengukuran merepresentasikan pengukuran basis standar:\n"
"qubit diubah ke keadaan pasca-pengukuran mereka, sementara hasil pengukuran *ditimpa* ke bit klasik yang ditunjuk oleh panah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It's often convenient to depict a measurement as a gate that takes a qubit as input and outputs a classical bit (as opposed to outputting the qubit in its post-measurement state and writing the result to a separate classical bit).\n"
"This means the measured qubit has been discarded and can safely be ignored thereafter, its state having changed into $\\vert 0\\rangle$ or $\\vert 1\\rangle$ depending upon the measurement outcome.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sering kali nyaman untuk menggambarkan pengukuran sebagai gate yang mengambil qubit sebagai masukan dan menghasilkan bit klasik (sebagai lawan dari menghasilkan qubit dalam keadaan pasca-pengukurannya dan menuliskan hasilnya ke bit klasik terpisah).\n"
"Ini berarti qubit yang diukur telah dibuang dan dapat diabaikan dengan aman setelahnya, keadaannya telah berubah menjadi $\\vert 0\\rangle$ atau $\\vert 1\\rangle$ tergantung pada hasil pengukuran.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, the following circuit diagram represents the same process as "
"the one in the previous diagram, but where we disregard $\\mathsf{X}$ and "
"$\\mathsf{Y}$ after measuring them:\n"
msgstr ""
"Misalnya, diagram circuit berikut merepresentasikan proses yang sama dengan "
"yang ada di diagram sebelumnya, tetapi di mana kita mengabaikan "
"$\\mathsf{X}$ dan $\\mathsf{Y}$ setelah mengukurnya:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Example circuit with measurements "
"compact](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-"
"circuits/ebit-circuit-measured-compact.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Contoh circuit dengan pengukuran kompak](/learning/images/courses/basics-"
"of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/ebit-circuit-measured-compact.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As the course continues, we'll see more examples of quantum circuits, which are usually more complicated than the simple examples above.\n"
"Here are some examples of symbols used to denote gates that commonly appear in circuit diagrams:\n"
msgstr ""
"Seiring kursus berlanjut, kita akan melihat lebih banyak contoh quantum circuit, yang biasanya lebih kompleks dari contoh sederhana di atas.\n"
"Berikut adalah beberapa contoh simbol yang digunakan untuk menunjukkan gate yang sering muncul dalam diagram circuit:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Single-qubit gates are generally shown as squares with a letter indicating "
"which operation it is, like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Gate qubit tunggal umumnya ditampilkan sebagai kotak dengan huruf yang "
"menunjukkan operasi apa itu, seperti ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  ![Single-qubit gates](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/quantum-circuits/single-qubit-gates.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"  ![Gate qubit tunggal](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/quantum-circuits/single-qubit-gates.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Not gates (or equivalently, $X$ gates) are also sometimes denoted by a "
"circle around a plus sign:\n"
msgstr ""
"  Gate NOT (atau setara, gate $X$) juga terkadang dilambangkan dengan "
"lingkaran di sekitar tanda plus:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  ![Not gate](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/quantum-circuits/not-gate.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"  ![Gate NOT](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/quantum-circuits/not-gate.svg)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Swap gates are denoted as follows:\n"
msgstr "Gate swap dilambangkan sebagai berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  ![Swap gate](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/quantum-circuits/swap-gate.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"  ![Gate swap](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/quantum-circuits/swap-gate.svg)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Controlled-gates, meaning gates that describe controlled-unitary operations, are denoted by a\n"
"filled-in circle (indicating the control) connected by a vertical line to whatever operation is being controlled. For instance, controlled-NOT gates, controlled-controlled-NOT (or Toffoli) gates, and controlled-swap (Fredkin) gates are denoted like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Gate terkontrol, yaitu gate yang menggambarkan operasi controlled-unitary, "
"dilambangkan dengan lingkaran berisi (menunjukkan kontrol) yang terhubung "
"oleh garis vertikal ke operasi apa pun yang dikendalikan. Misalnya, gate "
"controlled-NOT, gate controlled-controlled-NOT (atau Toffoli), dan gate "
"controlled-swap (Fredkin) dilambangkan seperti ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  ![Controlled gate](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/quantum-circuits/controlled-gates.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"  ![Gate terkontrol](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/quantum-circuits/controlled-gates.svg)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Arbitrary unitary operations on multiple qubits may be viewed as gates. They"
" are depicted by rectangles labeled by the name of the unitary operation. "
"For instance, here is a depiction of an (unspecified) unitary operation $U$ "
"as a gate, along with a controlled version of this gate:\n"
msgstr ""
"Operasi uniter sembarang pada beberapa qubit dapat dipandang sebagai gate. "
"Operasi tersebut digambarkan dengan persegi panjang yang diberi label nama "
"operasi uniter. Misalnya, berikut adalah penggambaran operasi uniter (tidak "
"ditentukan) $U$ sebagai gate, bersama dengan versi terkontrol dari gate "
"ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  ![Arbitrary unitary gate together with controlled "
"version](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-"
"circuits/uncontrolled-and-controlled-unitary.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"  ![Gate uniter sembarang bersama versi "
"terkontrol](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-"
"circuits/uncontrolled-and-controlled-unitary.svg)\n"
